    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] John Wesley preached a sermon \"On the death of the Rev Mr George Whitefield\" both here and at Whitefield's Tabernacle, Moorfields, in 1770.\n[2] George Whitefield ( ; 27 December [O.S. 16 December] 1714 30 September 1770), also spelled George Whitfield, was an English Anglican cleric who was one of the founders of Methodism and the evangelical movement.\n[3] He gained a large following and was always in demand for his sermons, which were greatly influenced by those of John Wesley and George Whitefield.\n[4] George Whitefield and John's brother Charles Wesley were also significant leaders in the movement."
